{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 100, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With e4 removed, node 3 relies on fewer inputs, so adding the input-to-output skip restores a much-needed residual path and gains more (exps 15-17 vs 11-14)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In parameter-poor pooling cells an extra identity path to the output dilutes the already weak features and hurts accuracy (exp 19), unlike conv cells where it helps."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the e3 skip when e4 is also absent removes most or all paths into the output node, causing much larger drops (exps 65, 67)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If e5 is already none, deleting e4 leaves the output fed only by e3 (or nothing), so the loss is far larger (exps 33, 34)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the e3 skip, e4 is a key output path and its removal hurts more (exps 32, 34 vs 31)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on a previously missing edge into the output gives more benefit than swapping an existing op (exps 92, 95, 97, 98 vs 91, 93, 94)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 1x1 conv with a 3x3 conv on e5 gives little or negative gain, while replacing none, skip, or pool gives clear gains (exp 3 vs 1, 2, 4)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When there is no direct input-to-output skip, a skip on e0 supplies a residual route through node 1, offsetting the conv loss (exp 87 vs 81-86)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e0 absent, e1 is the only route from the input into the deeper nodes, so replacing its conv with pooling is much more damaging (exp 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When e2 is none, node 1 feeds only e4, so strengthening e0 benefits fewer downstream paths and the gain shrinks (exps 25, 26 vs 21-24)."}], "tok": 32528, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x